pe="fig" rid="f2-ijms-9-6-0926">Scheme 1</xref> where the first entry is derived exclusively from calculated IPs and the second uses also the experimental IP(A) and IP(Hg) values of <xref ref-type="table" rid="t1-ijms-9-6-0926">Table 1</xref>.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t3-ijms-9-6-0926" position="float"><label>Table 3.</label><caption><p>Analysis of the Bond Density. <xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn4-ijms-9-6-0926">a</xref></p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Molecule</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Bond density &#x003c1;(r<sub>c</sub>) [e/&#x000c5;<sup>3</sup>]</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Energy density H(r<sub>c</sub>) [hartree/&#x000c5;<sup>3</sup>]</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Position of r<sub>c</sub> &#x00394;(Hg) [%]</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Atomic Charge Q(Hg) [melectron]</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">HgH (<sup>2</sup>&#x003a3;<sup>+</sup>)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.681</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;0.331</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;34.8</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">387</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">HgLi (<sup>2</sup>&#x003a3;<sup>+</sup>)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.069</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.004</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">37.7</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;306</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">HgNa (<sup>2</sup>&#x003a3;<sup>+</sup>)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.053</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.002</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">22.9</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;218</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">HgK (<sup>2</sup>&#x